                                "sense_id": "d21e72ca-4982-314c-9634-c035b0a6898f",
                                "text": "…such as Koffka’s allusion ¹ to some lectures on personality by Wertheimer, one of the leaders of the Gestalt psychology, that not all its representatives share the circumscribed view that we must preëmpt the problem of perception in all its diversified phases before we can venture forth on any other task.²"
                            },
                            {
